1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,997
No real process is ever truly reversible.

2
00:00:03,997 --> 00:00:10,000
Free expansion, burning fuel, rubbing your hands together: all irreversible.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,257
Reversibility is a limiting ideal, but it is a useful one, because it sets the best performance any real machine could ever approach.

